71:\label{sec:compl}
72:Algorithm {\sf BooleanSolve} deals with a large number of Macaulay matrices in degree~$d_0$. We first obtain bounds on the row and column dimensions of Macaulay matrices, as well as their number of nonzero entries, in terms of the degree. We then 
73:bound the witness degree by~$d_0$. The complexity analysis is concluded by optimizing the value of the ratio $k/n$ that governs the number of variables evaluated in the first exhaustive search.
